okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Back up a running agent session (conversation, Ciel session state, CLI settings, work files) and restore it later, on the same machine or another one; local and remote targets; manual, scheduled, event and MCP triggers."
reported: "User, 2026-10-09: '현재 에이전트가 동작하는 시점에서 세션을 저장하거나 백업해서 나중에 돌리기 혹은 원격지에 저장 및 백업할수잇는 솔류션이 필요해'. Answers: include conversation + Ciel state + work files + CLI settings ('언제든 새로 복원할수있는 모든 설정'); remote: all options; triggers: manual, periodic, events, MCP tool; restore: same machine and migration. Plan (C:\\Users\\djlov\\.claude\\plans\\temporal-enchanting-newt.md) approved through the session's plan hook. Docker test images: user allowed minio/minio, linuxserver/openssh-server, rclone/rclone."
design:
  format: "session_backup_store.py: manifest snapshots/<workspace>/<id>.json + content-addressed 8 MiB chunks blobs/<aa>/<sha256> (zlib). Unchanged chunks are not uploaded again; the manifest is written after every chunk."
  collect: "session_backup_collect.py: roots cwd, claude, home (~/.claude.json), codex, ciel, ciel_ws. Claude projects/<cwd key> transcripts + <sid>/ (subagents, tool-results), file-history, todos, settings; Codex threads of the cwd (state_*.sqlite, cwd stored as \\\\?\\C:\\... handled) with their rollouts, config, prompts, skills; Ciel workspace state, config.json, launch-state. jsonl read to the current size minus a partial last line; sqlite via the backup API. Work folder with default excludes."
  secrets: "session_backup_secrets.py: CLI sign-in files, Ciel vaults with their .key files, credential fields of JSON settings go only into a bundle encrypted with the operator's backup key (CIEL_RUNTIME_BACKUP_KEY / --key-file; scrypt + HMAC-SHA256 stream and tag, stdlib only). The key is never stored; without it the bundle is left out and only names are listed."
  targets: "session_backup_targets.py: local folder/UNC, ssh (sftp -b, key auth, optional known_hosts file), s3 (S3-compatible, SigV4, keys only as ${ENV} references), rclone (any remote). Settings in CONFIG_DIR/session-backup.json."
  restore: "session_backup_ops.py / session_backup_remap.py: refuses while the workspace's Ciel launcher pid runs (--force overrides), takes a pre-restore snapshot, writes atomically, merges secret fields back when the key is given. To another folder/user/machine: Claude project folder name, ~/.claude.json projects key, Codex threads cwd/rollout_path (extended-length form kept), config.toml [projects.\"<cwd>\"], launch-state key move to the new paths; conversation records keep their original paths."
  triggers: "session_backup_service.py: every automatic backup is a `backup create --prune` child process, one per workspace (pid lock). Router BackupScheduler (interval, only when session files changed; turn end via tui_observation.TURN_ENDED_LISTENERS, at most every min_interval), runtime_launch after the CLI exits (before_restart / on_session_end; Claude TUI, Codex TUI, Codex app-server/remote/desktop end), router MCP tool session_backup (create/list/status; no restore), menu 18. Session backup. All triggers default off. Retention keep_last + keep_daily; prune deletes only chunks no kept snapshot uses."
  cli: "ciel-runtime backup create|list|show|verify|restore|prune|schedule|status|target (cli_dispatch, lazy import). ciel_runtime.py stays at 4980 lines (scheduler start/stop added to the existing router service lines)."
tests:
  unit: "tests/test_session_backup.py (25 tests: collection, partial line, no secret in plain chunks/manifest, secrets without key, incremental upload, restore with secrets, restore to new layout without key, migration remap, extended-length cwd form, verify damage, CLI create/list/restore/verify, refuse while running, seal/open, split/merge, chunking, S3 signing/listing, scheduler interval/change/turn-end/default-off, turn-ended listener once, lock, after-exit gating, MCP dispatch, menu toggles, prune). Updated pins: test_channel_mcp_tools (tool set), menu position tests (dangerous-rm/oauth/request-limits), panel projection row 18."
  groups: "scripts/run_test_group.py, CIEL_RUNTIME_* unset: unit 1791 OK, runtime 398 OK, router 1175 OK, channel 457 OK; ruff clean. In the last full pass test_windows_conpty (Korean prompt) and two test_channel_transcript_repository boundary-scan tests failed once and passed on the immediate rerun; cause not investigated. Live router 9611 = 200 throughout. Real ~/.codex/config.toml and ~/.claude/.credentials.json were not touched by any run (E2E backup commands ran with a scratch USERPROFILE/HOME/CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR)."
e2e:
  e2e-1-remote-backup-restore: "Codex TUI + app-server, stub upstream. Turn A (ALPHA-7731) -> `backup create` while running (82 files, 80/82 chunks uploaded, 4.2 MB -> 410 KB compressed, secrets encrypted) -> turn B (BETA) still works -> stop -> wipe CODEX_HOME sessions/state/auth/history, the Ciel workspace state and the work file -> `backup restore` (safety snapshot taken, 82 written, secrets restored, work file back) -> relaunch --continue -> turn C (GAMMA): its request carries ALPHA and not BETA (BETA came after the snapshot); shots/05-L2-turnC.png shows turn A and turn C in the restored TUI. The script's RESULT line first read False because it judged the title-generation request; the judge was fixed, the bodies (n=5 has_alpha/has_gamma True) are in driver.log. Test API key not in plain chunks; passphrase not in any backup file."
  e2e-2-remote-targets: "Same session to ssh (linuxserver/openssh-server on 127.0.0.1:2222, test key, own known_hosts), s3 (rclone serve s3 on 127.0.0.1:18080; minio images were not pullable: 'pull access denied' / quay 401), rclone (rclone/rclone:1.71.1 through rclone_docker.py). Each: target add, create (80/82 chunks), second create after an edit (2 chunks), list, verify ok, restore into an empty layout (82 files, secrets restored). Restored files equal the source except the work file edited after the snapshot and the two sqlite files, whose table contents are equal (backup API copies are not byte-identical)."
  e2e-3-migrate-triggers: "e2e-1's snapshot restored to new cwd/CODEX_HOME/Ciel dir/home (Codex thread cwd remapped; the first attempt failed to continue because the \\\\?\\ form was not recognised -> fixed). `--continue` in the new folder: turn C request carries ALPHA from the original folder. With on_turn_end/before_restart/on_session_end on: turn-end snapshot, MCP tools/call session_backup create (snapshot) and status, `ciel-runtime restart-session` -> pre-restart snapshot, Codex back, next turns -> turn-end snapshots."
  e2e-4-session-end-menu: "Ctrl+C twice ends Codex -> session-end snapshot (twice, driver-session-end.log). Menu (--ca-menu): row '18. Session backup [schedule off · last … ok]'; panel opened; 'Scheduled backups' toggled on -> session-backup.json schedule.enabled true, row 18 shows 'every 60 min' (shots/22-panel-schedule-toggled.png)."
incidents:
  - "A stopped earlier run of e2e_migrate_triggers.py kept running (TaskStop ended the shell, not the python child) and tore down the same test paths at 22:26:49, so that run's session-end and menu steps are void; they were rerun alone as e2e-4. driver.log of e2e-3 holds lines of both runs; only 22:24 onward belong to the valid run."
  - "SendKeys '/quit' went through the desktop's Korean IME ('/벼ㅑㅅ'); the harness now quits with Ctrl+C. Early menu key attempts changed the scratch config's log level to ERROR (test config only)."
cleanup: "Test containers ciel-e2e-ssh and ciel-e2e-s3 removed. Images linuxserver/openssh-server and rclone/rclone:1.71.1 remain pulled. Scratch (configs, homes, test SSH key, backups) is in the session scratchpad, not in the repo."
not_verified:
  - "Claude Code session end to end (collection, restore and remap of Claude projects are unit-tested only)."
  - "Periodic schedule firing in a live router (tick logic unit-tested; the router scheduler thread started, shown by its turn-end listener working)."
  - "Real cloud accounts (AWS S3, Google Drive via rclone); only local compatible servers."
  - "Restore across real machines/OS users (.14 etc.); migration was across folders on this PC."
  - "Prune races with a snapshot of another workspace being written to the same target at the same time (chunks a running backup reuses could be removed if their last kept user is pruned)."
not_done: "Not committed, not pushed, not deployed to any agent."
